Refresh the access token using stored credentials

  Re-mints the access token without a full browser login. Client-credentials
  profiles re-run the client-credentials grant. Authorization-code profiles
  force a refresh-token exchange using the stored refresh token.

  If your permissions changed (for example new roles were added), you may
  still need to run 'ags auth login' again for them to take effect.

  With --format json, outputs the refreshed status, base URL, client ID, and
  token expiry.

Usage:
  auth refresh

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
